source:
Tom and Katie are discussing whether simultaneous equations are in an appropriate form to be added or subtracted, or whether they need transforming first. Tom says these equations are in an appropriate form
\(
\begin{array}{l}
2 x-3 y=10 \\
5 x+3 y=18
\end{array}
\) Katie says these equations are in an appropriate form
\(
\begin{array}{l}
2 x-3 y=10 \\
2 x+y=4
\end{array}
\) Who is correct?

translation:
汤姆和凯蒂正在讨论，这些联立方程是否可以直接进行加法或减法运算，或者是否需要先进行变换。汤姆说，这些方程的形式是合适的。
\(
\begin{array}{l}
2 x-3 y=10 \\
5 x+3 y=18
\end{array}
\) 凯蒂说，这些方程的形式是合适的。
\(
\begin{array}{l}
2 x-3 y=10 \\
2 x+y=4
\end{array}
\) 谁说得对？

